  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Daily showers/thunderstorm chances continue this week.\n\n- Warmer latter half of this week, then return to seasonable\n  temperatures this weekend.\n\n\nAn active convective pattern is imminent through the rest of this\nweek as an upper-level low meanders through California and the\nGreat Basin, allowing deep southerly flow to transport moisture \nacross the Northern Rockies.\n\nToday through Friday, the overall stagnant pattern yields little\nday-to-day change, keeping daily afternoon showers and\nthunderstorms in the forecast. Model trends suggest increasing\ninstability but weaker deep-layer shear on today and tomorrow,\nwith less shower/thunderstorm coverage overall. However, a\nlocalized severe weather threat will persist and will expand back\ninto north-central Idaho. Daytime temperatures will warm to well\nabove normal levels once again. \n\nFor the weekend, ensemble clusters are in good agreement that the\nupper low will lift northeastward on Friday, reaching the\nYellowstone region by Saturday and maintaining daily shower and\nthunderstorm chances. A weak cold front on Friday will temporarily\nreturn temperatures to seasonal averages for the weekend before a\nbuilding ridge early next week drives temperatures back above\nnormal.",
